      "artist": "UN  International Criminal Tribunal for the former Yugoslavia",
      "description": "Since its establishment, it was the Tribunal’s goal for the proceedings to be public and transparent while conducted in accordance with the highest international human rights standards, respecting both the rights of the accused and the dignity of all other participants in the proceedings, primarily the witnesses. \n\nWhen the Tribunal was established in 1993, most national jurisdictions did not broadcast criminal trials nor a need to translate their proceedings into two languages, let alone four. Thanks to its state-of-the-art courtroom technology, the Tribunal is able to bring its proceedings in The Hague to the people of the former Yugoslavia and to the world.",
      "dateCreated": "2013-05-16 14:50",
